{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-69316",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The sum of cubes formula is given by\n\n$$\n{a}^{3}+{b}^{3}=(a+b)({a}^{2}-ab+{b}^{2}).\n$$\n\nNotice that we can write our expression as a sum of cubes, as follows:\n\n$$\n{p}^{3}+27={p}^{3}+{3}^{3}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor our expression using the sum of cubes formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{p}^{3}+27 & ={p}^{3}+{3}^{3} \\\\  & =(p+3)({p}^{2}-p\\cdot 3+{3}^{2}) \\\\  & =(p+3)({p}^{2}-3p+9)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
